{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UTFhLTAo76TGcurHtoy6UZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Exit collapse + routing gradient 保持为 core findings（reviewer acceptance\n2\t  ~75%）， CF sensitivity 降为 \"supporting evidence with caveats\"（acceptance ~45%）。 1-2\n3\t  位 reviewer 指出 metric incomparability（trained Cohen''s d vs untrained cosine dist）\n4\t  使 amplification 的定量化不可靠，要求 behavioral validation 作为 representational claims 的补充。\n5\t  Rebuttal 需要：(1) Δ>0.10 阈值 sensitivity analysis，(2) 诚实回应 behavioral gap， (3) 将 CF\n6\t  从 \"core finding\" 重新定位为 \"consistent observation\"。 预计 reviewer_avg ~6.0，accept_prob\n7\t  ~0.35，rebuttal_success ~0.50。\n8\t\n9\t  '\n10\timagined_experiments:\n11\t- name: SigLIP+Projector RSA baseline\n12\t  plan_id: plan_001\n13\t  description: SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO — 证明 action-relevant 结构源自\n14\t    frozen vision encoder\n15\t  expected_results:\n16\t    siglip_projector_rsa: 0.6153\n17\t    bootstrap_95_ci:\n18\t    - 0.5257\n19\t    - 0.6954\n20\t    trained_vla_peak_rsa: 0.4876\n21\t    untrained_vla_peak_rsa: 0.4846\n22\t    dino_rsa: 0.388\n23\t    llm_degradation_magnitude: 0.127\n24\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档位下此实验被全部 reviewer 接受（A1 holds）。RSA=0.615 >> VLA 0.488\n25\t    的 gap 清晰建立了 \"vision encoder 是 action-relevant structure 的主要来源\" 这一非争议性结论。 但 1 位\n26\t    reviewer 会注意到这是 RSA metric 下的结论——CKA 下 ordering 不同（plan_009 结果）。 此实验对 C1 framework\n27\t    贡献最大，不涉及 median 档位的核心争议点（CF metric incomparability）。 CI 较宽 [0.526, 0.695] 会被提及但不作为\n28\t    major concern，因为 point estimate 远高于 VLA peak。\n29\t\n30\t    '\n31\t  tables:\n32\t  - title: Action-Relevant Structure Source Decomposition\n33\t    columns:\n34\t    - Representation\n35\t    - RSA (ρ)\n36\t    - 95% CI\n37\t    - vs DINO\n38\t    rows:\n39\t    - - SigLIP+Projector\n40\t      - '0.615'\n41\t      - '[0.526, 0.695]'\n42\t      - '+0.227'\n43\t    - - VLA Trained Peak (L9)\n44\t      - '0.488'\n45\t      - —\n46\t      - '+0.100'\n47\t    - - VLA Untrained Peak (L12)\n48\t      - '0.485'\n49\t      - —\n50\t      - '+0.097'\n51\t    - - DINO cls_token\n52\t      - '0.388'\n53\t      - —\n54\t      - baseline\n55\t  figures_description:\n56\t  - 'Bar chart: RSA values for SigLIP projector > VLA trained ≈ VLA untrained >> DINO,\n57\t    with 95% CI error bars。清晰的三级阶梯。'\n58\t  analysis: 'Reviewer 共识：frozen encoder dominance 不争议。但 median 档位下 Reviewer 2 可能指出\n59\t    \"LLM degradation\" 的措辞过强——LLM 同时在做 instruction routing 和 action computation， RSA\n60\t    下降可能反映功能转换而非信息丢失。建议用 \"geometric reorganization\" 替代 \"degradation\"。 此实验在 rebuttal\n61\t    中无需调整。\n62\t\n63\t    '\n64\t- name: DINO standalone baseline\n65\t  plan_id: plan_002\n66\t  description: DINOv2 baseline RSA — standalone vision model 参照\n67\t  expected_results:\n68\t    temporal_distance_rho_pooled: 0.833\n69\t    per_task_rho_mean: 0.9008\n70\t    R2: 0.687\n71\t    subtask_macro_auc: 0.9717\n72\t    control_b_permutation_rho: 0.039\n73\t  result_rationale: 'Clean baseline，无争议。DINO RSA=0.388 远低于 VLA 和 projector，建立了 architecture\n74\t    gap。 Subtask AUC=0.97 被 reviewer 接受但会引发 \"goals are visually distinguishable\" 的注意，\n75\t    这在后续 goal classification experiments 中成为 confound（10-way classification trivially\n76\t    easy）。 Median 档位下此实验本身不受挑战，但 reviewer 会用它来质疑后续 probe 实验的 discriminability。\n77\t\n78\t    '\n79\t  tables:\n80\t  - title: DINOv2 Standalone Performance\n81\t    columns:\n82\t    - Metric\n83\t    - Value\n84\t    - Note\n85\t    rows:\n86\t    - - Temporal ρ (per-task)\n87\t      - '0.901'\n88\t      - correct baseline\n89\t    - - Action Probe R²\n90\t      - '0.687'\n91\t      - vision-only ceiling\n92\t    - - Subtask AUC\n93\t      - '0.972'\n94\t      - visually distinguishable\n95\t    - - Permutation Control ρ\n96\t      - '0.039'\n97\t      - validates signal\n98\t  figures_description:\n99\t  - 'Scatter: predicted vs actual temporal distance，per-task colored。High correlation\n100\t    but cross-task variance visible。'\n101\t  analysis: '所有 reviewer 接受。用于建立 DINO < SigLIP < VLA trained 的 ordering baseline。\n102\t    Median 档位下唯一风险：Reviewer 3 可能质疑 DINOv2 作为 baseline 的 fairness （DINOv2 是 ViT-L/14\n103\t    1024d vs VLA 4096d），但 dimension mismatch 在 RSA/CKA 中 不是 confound（metric 对 dimensionality\n104\t    invariant）。\n105\t\n106\t    '\n107\t- name: Per-layer RSA degradation curve\n108\t  plan_id: plan_003\n109\t  description: Per-layer RSA curve — 追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的变换轨迹\n110\t  expected_results:\n111\t    trained_image_mean_peak_layer: 9\n112\t    trained_image_mean_peak_rsa: 0.4876\n113\t    untrained_image_mean_peak_layer: 12\n114\t    untrained_image_mean_peak_rsa: 0.4846\n115\t    proj_to_l1_drop_trained: 0.2036\n116\t    proj_to_l1_drop_untrained: 0.1512\n117\t    trained_pattern: non_monotonic (inverted-U)\n118\t    untrained_pattern: non_monotonic\n119\t  result_rationale: 'Inverted-U pattern 是 C3 的核心 evidence。Median 档位下（A3 fails 的延伸）：\n120\t    (1) rise phase Δρ=+0.016 被 1 位 reviewer 认为 negligible（CI includes 0）， inverted-U\n121\t    的 \"rise\" 部分可能只是 noise； (2) CKA 下 pattern 完全不同（monotonic），reviewer 质疑 \"non-monotonic\n122\t    refinement\"  是 metric-specific artifact； (3) decline phase Δρ=-0.206 更 robust，但\n123\t    reviewer 要求在正文（非 appendix）承认 metric dependence。 最终 C3 作为 \"qualified observation\n124\t    under RSA\" 存活，但不贡献于 core claims。\n125\t\n126\t    '\n127\t  tables:\n128\t  - title: Per-Layer RSA Profile Summary\n129\t    columns:\n130\t    - Condition\n131\t    - Peak Layer\n132\t    - Peak RSA\n133\t    - Proj→L1 Drop\n134\t    - Pattern\n135\t    rows:\n136\t    - - Trained (with inst)\n137\t      - L9\n138\t      - '0.488'\n139\t      - '-0.204'\n140\t      - inverted-U\n141\t    - - Untrained (with inst)\n142\t      - L12\n143\t      - '0.485'\n144\t      - '-0.151'\n145\t      - non-monotonic\n146\t    - - Trained (no inst)\n147\t      - L30\n148\t      - '0.489'\n149\t      - '-0.253'\n150\t      - increasing\n151\t    - - Untrained (no inst)\n152\t      - L6\n153\t      - '0.480'\n154\t      - '-0.137'\n155\t      - non-monotonic\n156\t  figures_description:\n157\t  - '33-layer RSA profile plot: 4 conditions overlaid。Trained shows inverted-U with\n158\t    peak at L9-L12, untrained flatter。Projector output (0.615) as horizontal dashed\n159\t    line shows all LLM layers below projector。'\n160\t  analysis: 'Median 档位 Reviewer 2 的典型批评：\"The inverted-U pattern is only demonstrated\n161\t    under RSA.  CKA shows monotonic increase (plan_009), which directly contradicts\n162\t    the ''non-monotonic refinement''  narrative. The authors should either demonstrate\n163\t    metric-robustness or downgrade this to an observation.\" Response：承认并降级为 observation。Rebuttal\n164\t    可补充 R² functional probe 也显示 inverted-U （plan_011），但 reviewer 可能 counter：\"R² measures\n165\t    decodability, not geometry — different construct。\"\n166\t\n167\t    '\n168\t- name: Output head analysis (frozen encoder verification)\n169\t  plan_id: plan_004\n170\t  description: SigLIP+projector frozen 确认, LLM 权重变化不传导到视觉表征\n171\t  expected_results:\n172\t    vision_cos_sim: 1.0\n173\t    vision_rel_change: 0.0\n174\t    projector_cos_sim: 1.001\n175\t    projector_rel_change: 0.0\n176\t    llm_mean_rel_change: 1.316\n177\t    llm_range:\n178\t    - 1.22\n179\t    - 1.37\n180\t    head_vs_llm_ratio: 1.12\n181\t    shallow_adaptation_gate: FAIL (1.12x < 3x threshold)\n182\t  result_rationale: '此实验确认 vision backbone + projector 在 trained 和 untrained 之间完全一致（cos_sim=1.0），\n183\t    解释了为什么 RSA 在 image_mean tokens 上 trained ≈ untrained。Median 档位下被接受 （A1 holds），但\n184\t    reviewer 注意到 caveat：\"comparison is pretrained Llama vs random init,  not pre/post\n185\t    fine-tuning\"，这限制了 interpretability。LLM weights uniformly distributed （ratio=1.12x）否定了\n186\t    shallow adaptation hypothesis——head 不特殊。 此实验支持 C1 framework 的 \"frozen encoder\"\n187\t    前提，不涉及 median 档位的争议点。\n188\t\n189\t    '\n190\t  tables:\n191\t  - title: Weight Divergence by Module Group\n192\t    columns:\n193\t    - Module\n194\t    - Count\n195\t    - Mean Rel Change\n196\t    - Cos Sim\n197\t    - Verdict\n198\t    rows:\n199\t    - - Vision Backbone\n200\t      - '685'\n201\t      - '0.000'\n202\t      - '1.000'\n203\t      - IDENTICAL\n204\t    - - Projector\n205\t      - '6'\n206\t      - '0.000'\n207\t      - '1.001'\n208\t      - IDENTICAL\n209\t    - - LLM Layers\n210\t      - '288'\n211\t      - '1.316'\n212\t      - '0.218'\n213\t      - DIVERGED\n214\t    - - LM Head\n215\t      - '1'\n216\t      - '1.475'\n217\t      - '0.000'\n218\t      - DIVERGED\n219\t    - - Embedding\n220\t      - '1'\n221\t      - '1.329'\n222\t      - '-0.000'\n223\t      - DIVERGED\n224\t  figures_description:\n225\t  - 'Heatmap: rel_change per LLM layer (L0-L31)，showing uniform ~1.3 across all layers，no\n226\t    depth gradient。Vision/projector rows blank (zero change)。'\n227\t  analysis: '全部 reviewer 接受。此实验为 C1 framework 提供了必要的 architectural verification。 Median\n228\t    档位下无额外挑战。但 Reviewer 1 可能在 minor comments 中建议 \"clarify that  untrained = random\n229\t    init, not ablated weights\" 以避免读者误解。\n230\t\n231\t    '\n232\t- name: 6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks (orphaned)\n233\t  plan_id: plan_005\n234\t  description: 系统性验证 trained ≈ untrained across 6 methods\n235\t  expected_results:\n236\t    status: orphaned\n237\t    conclusion: 'All 6 methods consistent: trained ≈ untrained >> DINO'\n238\t    note: 被后续更精细的实验取代（plan_011 fulllayer R², d041 definitive RSA, etc.）\n239\t  result_rationale: '此实验在 Phase 1 被 orphaned，其核心结论（trained ≈ untrained in RSA/R²）被后续实验\n240\t    独立复现。在 median 档位下不直接贡献，但其 \"trained ≈ untrained\" 的 RSA 结论正是 reviewer 用来质疑 \"training\n241\t    effect\" narrative 的弹药之一——如果 training 不改变 RSA， 那 training 到底做了什么？Answer 在 C2（routing\n242\t    reorganization），但 reviewer 可能认为 证据不够 conclusive without behavioral validation（A4\n243\t    partially fails）。\n244\t\n245\t    '\n246\t  tables: []\n247\t  figures_description: []\n248\t  analysis: 'Orphaned，不进入论文。但其结论（trained ≈ untrained）被 plan_007 和 d041 复现， 成为 C3 \"observation\"\n249\t    而非 \"finding\" 的证据基础。\n250\t\n251\t    '\n252\t- name: Instruction ablation RSA\n253\t  plan_id: plan_006\n254\t  description: 去掉 instruction text 测 RSA 变化\n255\t  expected_results:\n256\t    with_inst_untrained_peak_rsa: 0.4846\n257\t    no_inst_untrained_peak_rsa: 0.4802\n258\t    delta: 0.0044\n259\t    gate_threshold: 0.1\n260\t    gate_judgment: FAIL — Δ=0.004 << 0.10\n261\t  result_rationale: 'Negative result：移除 instruction 对 image token RSA 几乎无影响（Δ=0.004\n262\t    << 0.10）。 这证明了 action-relevant structure 是 vision-driven 而非 instruction-driven。\n263\t    Median 档位下此结论被接受（支持 C1 \"image tokens 不 attend to instructions\" 的验证）， 但 reviewer\n264\t    可能指出：这只说明 image_mean RSA 不依赖 instruction，不能推广到 last_preaction tokens（C2 的核心 readout\n265\t    position）。实际上 last_preaction 的 routing 完全依赖 instruction（cross-instruction probe\n266\t    100%），两个 readout 位置的 independence pattern 不同——这本身是一个 finding，但需要在论文中明确区分。\n267\t\n268\t    '\n269\t  tables:\n270\t  - title: Instruction Ablation Effect on RSA\n271\t    columns:\n272\t    - Condition\n273\t    - Peak RSA\n274\t    - Δ vs with-inst\n275\t    rows:\n276\t    - - Untrained + instruction\n277\t      - '0.485'\n278\t      - baseline\n279\t    - - Untrained − instruction\n280\t      - '0.480'\n281\t      - '-0.004'\n282\t    - - Threshold for significance\n283\t      - —\n284\t      - '0.10'\n285\t    - - DINO baseline\n286\t      - '0.388'\n287\t      - —\n288\t  figures_description:\n289\t  - 'Per-layer RSA curves: with-instruction vs without-instruction overlay，几乎完全重合。DINO\n290\t    horizontal line 远低于两者。'\n291\t  analysis: 'Reviewer 接受。此 negative result 实际强化了 C1：image tokens 的 action-relevant  geometry\n292\t    来自 visual content，instruction presence 不影响。但 median 档位下  Reviewer 2 会追问：\"if instruction\n293\t    doesn''t matter for image tokens, what exactly  does VLA training change?\" — 这个问题的答案在\n294\t    C2（routing at instruction token positions）， 但需要更清晰的 framing。\n295\t\n296\t    '\n297\t- name: 2×2 training × instruction matrix\n298\t  plan_id: plan_007\n299\t  description: 四条件全收敛验证 — trained/untrained × with/without instruction\n300\t  expected_results:\n301\t    trained_with_inst: 0.4876\n302\t    trained_no_inst: 0.489\n303\t    untrained_with_inst: 0.4846\n304\t    untrained_no_inst: 0.4802\n305\t    bootstrap_delta_ci: '[-0.058, 0.072] includes 0'\n306\t    max_pairwise_delta: 0.0088\n307\t    dino_baseline: 0.388\n308\t  result_rationale: \"2×2 matrix 所有 4 cells 收敛在 0.480-0.489 的窄带中，bootstrap CI 包含 0。\\\n309\t    \\ 这是 C3 \\\"instruction invariance\\\" observation 的定量基础。Median 档位下被接受 但 reviewer\\\n310\t    \\ 的解读分歧： - Reviewer 1：接受，认为 \\\"vision encoder geometry dominates\\\" 是 clean result\\\n311\t    \\ - Reviewer 2：认为这意味着 \\\"neither training nor instruction has meaningful effect\\\n312\t    \\ \\n  on image token geometry\\\"，进而质疑论文的 novelty——如果训练不改变 RSA，论文需要\\n  更强地论证 routing/R²\\\n313\t    \\ 变化的意义\\n- Reviewer 3：接受，但要求将此与 C2 的 exit collapse（R² 层面的变化）明确对比——\\n  RSA 不变但\\\n314\t    \\ R² 变化说明 \\\"geometry preserved but decodability reorganized\\\"\\n\"\n315\t  tables:\n316\t  - title: '2×2 Factorial Design: RSA Convergence'\n317\t    columns:\n318\t    - ''\n319\t    - With Instruction\n320\t    - Without Instruction\n321\t    - Instruction Effect\n322\t    rows:\n323\t    - - Trained\n324\t      - '0.488'\n325\t      - '0.489'\n326\t      - '-0.001'\n327\t    - - Untrained\n328\t      - '0.485'\n329\t      - '0.480'\n330\t      - '+0.004'\n331\t    - - Training Effect\n332\t      - '+0.003'\n333\t      - '+0.009'\n334\t      - —\n335\t  figures_description:\n336\t  - '2×2 interaction plot: RSA on y-axis (range 0.47-0.50), training on x-axis, instruction\n337\t    as separate lines。Lines nearly flat and overlapping — no main effects, no interaction。DINO\n338\t    at 0.388 shown as reference。'\n339\t  analysis: 'Median 档位的关键 pivot point。此实验的 \"null result\"（4 条件无差异）在 median  scenario\n340\t    下被部分 reviewer 视为 limitation：\"if your framework can''t detect training  effects\n341\t    in RSA, perhaps RSA is the wrong metric。\" 这直接导致 C3 从 core claim  降为 observation。Rebuttal\n342\t    需要论证：RSA invariance + R² divergence = geometry-function  dissociation，这本身是 interesting，但需要\n343\t    behavioral evidence 来确认 functional significance。\n344\t\n345\t    '\n346\t- name: Random instruction control (content invariance)\n347\t  plan_id: plan_008\n348\t  description: 用 random/shuffled/empty instruction 替代真实 instruction 测 RSA 变化\n349\t  expected_results:\n350\t    normal_peak_rsa: 0.4888\n351\t    random_peak_rsa: 0.4835\n352\t    shuffled_peak_rsa: 0.4832\n353\t    empty_peak_rsa: 0.4723\n354\t    max_absolute_delta: 0.0165\n355\t    instruction_invariant: true\n356\t  result_rationale: '三重不变性完备验证：training invariance（plan_007）+ instruction presence\n357\t    invariance （plan_006）+ instruction content invariance（此实验）。所有 delta < 0.017。 Median\n358\t    档位下被全部 reviewer 接受为 thorough control。这实际上强化了 C1 framework 的可信度——image token geometry\n359\t    对 instruction content 完全不敏感。 但 reviewer 会对比 counterfactual sensitivity results（C2-X\n360\t    CF）：image tokens 对 instruction invariant，但 instruction/last_preaction tokens 高度\n361\t    sensitive（d≥0.45）。 这个 dissociation 本身是 interesting，但在 median 档位下被认为 \"consistent\n362\t    with  causal mask — not surprising。\"\n363\t\n364\t    '\n365\t  tables:\n366\t  - title: Instruction Content Invariance (Trained Model)\n367\t    columns:\n368\t    - Instruction Type\n369\t    - Peak RSA\n370\t    - Δ vs Normal\n371\t    rows:\n372\t    - - Normal (correct)\n373\t      - '0.489'\n374\t      - baseline\n375\t    - - Random tokens\n376\t      - '0.484'\n377\t      - '-0.005'\n378\t    - - Shuffled words\n379\t      - '0.483'\n380\t      - '-0.006'\n381\t    - - Empty string\n382\t      - '0.472'\n383\t      - '-0.017'\n384\t  figures_description:\n385\t  - 'Per-layer RSA curves: 4 instruction conditions overlaid。All curves within ±0.017\n386\t    band。Peak layers identical (L16)。'\n387\t  analysis: 'Uncontroversial control。所有 reviewer 认为此实验 demonstrates thoroughness。\n388\t    Median 档位下唯一 minor concern：empty string Δ=-0.017 是 4 条件中最大的， 暗示 instruction presence\n389\t    有微弱效应（token count/position effect），但远低于 threshold。\n390\t\n391\t    '\n392\t- name: CKA verification (metric robustness)\n393\t  plan_id: plan_009\n394\t  description: 用 CKA 指标重复 RSA 发现，确保不是指标依赖\n395\t  expected_results:\n396\t    linear_cka_ordering: untrained > trained > projector > DINO\n397\t    rdm_cka_ordering: trained > projector > untrained > DINO\n398\t    rsa_ordering: projector >> trained ≈ untrained >> DINO\n399\t    cka_reversal_detected: true\n400\t    dino_lowest_robust: true\n401\t    last_preaction_highest: 0.127\n402\t  result_rationale: '这是 median 档位的关键 problematic experiment。CKA ordering 与 RSA 反转——\n403\t    CKA 下 untrained > trained（RSA 下 trained ≈ untrained），projector 不再最高。 这直接导致： (1)\n404\t    C3 的 \"non-monotonic refinement\" 仅在 RSA 下成立，metric-dependent； (2) DINOv2 \"highest\n405\t    geometric foundation\" 仅在 RSA 下成立； (3) 1-2 位 reviewer 认为 RSA 结果不可推广。 但 DINO 在所有\n406\t    metrics 下均最低（robust），且 last_preaction >> image_mean 的 redistribution pattern 在\n407\t    CKA 下也成立。 A2 partially 的表现：exit collapse 主要基于 R²（functional metric），不依赖 RSA/CKA，\n408\t    所以 exit collapse 本身不受 CKA reversal 影响。但 C3 vision encoder geometry claim  被严重\n409\t    undercut。\n410\t\n411\t    '\n412\t  tables:\n413\t  - title: RSA vs CKA Metric Comparison\n414\t    columns:\n415\t    - Representation\n416\t    - RSA (ρ)\n417\t    - Linear CKA\n418\t    - RDM-CKA\n419\t    - Consistent?\n420\t    rows:\n421\t    - - SigLIP Projector\n422\t      - '0.615'\n423\t      - '0.081'\n424\t      - '0.257'\n425\t      - No — RSA >> CKA\n426\t    - - VLA Trained (img_mean)\n427\t      - '0.488'\n428\t      - '0.083'\n429\t      - '0.260'\n430\t      - 'No'\n431\t    - - VLA Untrained (img_mean)\n432\t      - '0.485'\n433\t      - '0.089'\n434\t      - '0.246'\n435\t      - No — CKA reversal\n436\t    - - DINO cls_token\n437\t      - '0.388'\n438\t      - '0.066'\n439\t      - '0.241'\n440\t      - Yes — lowest in all\n441\t    - - VLA Trained (last_pre)\n442\t      - —\n443\t      - '0.127'\n444\t      - '0.290'\n445\t      - Highest in CKA\n446\t  figures_description:\n447\t  - 'Side-by-side bar charts: RSA ordering (projector > trained ≈ untrained > DINO)\n448\t    vs CKA ordering (untrained > trained > projector > DINO for linear CKA)。Visual\n449\t    对比 highlights reversal。'\n450\t  analysis: 'Median 档位核心 attack surface。Reviewer 2 的典型评论： \"The RSA-CKA dissociation\n451\t    undermines confidence in the geometric interpretation.  The authors claim ''non-monotonic\n452\t    refinement'' based on RSA, but CKA shows monotonic  structure. This metric dependence\n453\t    should be acknowledged as a fundamental limitation,  not relegated to an appendix.\"\n454\t    Rebuttal 策略：承认 dissociation，将 C3 降为 \"observation under RSA\"，强调 C2 （exit collapse,\n455\t    routing）基于 R² functional probe，不依赖 RSA/CKA 选择。 Reviewer acceptance for C3 drops\n456\t    to ~0.4，但 C2 不受影响（~0.75）。\n457\t\n458\t    '\n459\t- name: LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark replication\n460\t  plan_id: plan_010\n461\t  description: 第三个 benchmark 交叉验证 RSA inverted-U 和 R² patterns\n462\t  expected_results:\n463\t    rsa_trained_img_peak:\n464\t      layer: 14\n465\t      rsa: 0.691\n466\t    rsa_trained_lastpre_peak:\n467\t      layer: 15\n468\t      rsa: 0.695\n469\t    rsa_untrained_img_peak:\n470\t      layer: 0\n471\t      rsa: 0.652\n472\t    r2_trained_img_peak:\n473\t      layer: 13\n474\t      R2: 0.696\n475\t    r2_trained_lastpre_peak:\n476\t      layer: 21\n477\t      R2: 0.675\n478\t    r2_untrained_img_peak:\n479\t      layer: 0\n480\t      R2: 0.673\n481\t    bootstrap_p: <0.001 for all trained vs untrained\n482\t    cross_benchmark_consistency: high — peak layers within 2-layer range\n483\t  result_rationale: 'LIBERO-Spatial 复现了 LIBERO-Goal 的所有核心 patterns：trained inverted-U,  untrained\n484\t    flat/declining, bootstrap significant。Peak layers 一致（Goal L8-L13,  Spatial L13-L21）。Median\n485\t    档位下此实验强化了 within-OpenVLA 的 reproducibility， 被 reviewer 接受。但 reviewer 会注意到： (1)\n486\t    仍然是同一架构（OpenVLA），跨架构验证更重要（D088-D094 addresses this）； (2) RSA inverted-U 的 rise\n487\t    phase 在 Spatial 中 Δρ=0.039（Goal 中 0.016）， 略更 robust 但仍在 metric-dependent 的质疑范围内。\n488\t\n489\t    '\n490\t  tables:\n491\t  - title: Cross-Benchmark Replication (Goal vs Spatial)\n492\t    columns:\n493\t    - Metric\n494\t    - Goal Peak\n495\t    - Spatial Peak\n496\t    - Δ Layers\n497\t    rows:\n498\t    - - RSA trained img_mean\n499\t      - L12 (0.628)\n500\t      - L14 (0.691)\n501\t      - '+2'\n502\t    - - RSA trained last_pre\n503\t      - L12 (0.643)\n504\t      - L15 (0.695)\n505\t      - '+3'\n506\t    - - R² trained img_mean\n507\t      - L8 (0.655)\n508\t      - L13 (0.696)\n509\t      - '+5'\n510\t    - - R² trained last_pre\n511\t      - L13 (0.678)\n512\t      - L21 (0.675)\n513\t      - '+8'\n514\t  figures_description:\n515\t  - 'Dual-panel per-layer profile: Goal (left) vs Spatial (right), with RSA and R²\n516\t    curves overlaid。Both show inverted-U for trained condition。Peak layers marked\n517\t    with vertical lines。'\n518\t  analysis: 'Reviewer 接受 cross-benchmark replication。Median 档位下 Reviewer 1 可能评价： \"Good\n519\t    that patterns replicate across task suites, but both are within the same  model\n520\t    (OpenVLA). The cross-architecture validation (TracVLA, NORA) is more convincing  for\n521\t    the generalization claim.\" 此实验对 A1 holds 贡献但不是 decisive。\n522\t\n523\t    '\n524\t- name: Full-layer R² scan (132 probes)\n525\t  plan_id: plan_011\n526\t  description: 33 layers × 2 conditions × 2 aggregations — R² per-layer curve 验证 exit\n527\t    collapse\n528\t  expected_results:\n529\t    trained_image_mean_peak:\n530\t      layer: 8\n531\t      R2: 0.6553\n532\t    trained_last_preaction_peak:\n533\t      layer: 13\n534\t      R2: 0.6779\n535\t    untrained_image_mean_peak:\n536\t      layer: 0\n537\t      R2: 0.6403\n538\t    untrained_last_preaction_peak:\n539\t      layer: 32\n540\t      R2: 0.6093\n541\t    bootstrap_best_vs_best_imgmean:\n542\t      delta: 0.015\n543\t      p: 0.006\n544\t    bootstrap_best_vs_best_lastpre:\n545\t      delta: 0.069\n546\t      p: 0.0001\n547\t    untrained_L10_L13_collapse: R² near -0.33 (pathological)\n548\t  result_rationale: \"此实验是 C2 exit collapse 的 foundational evidence（OpenVLA 内部）。 Trained\\\n549\t    \\ last_preaction 显示经典 inverted-U：L13 peak 0.678 → L32 exit 0.609（Δ=0.069）。 Untrained\\\n550\t    \\ 则 L10-L13 完全 collapse（R² ≈ -0.33），仅 L32 恢复到 0.609。\\nMedian 档位下（A2 partially）：\\\n551\t    \\ - Exit collapse pattern 被接受（3/4 reviewers） - 但 Reviewer 3 质疑 Δ>0.10 阈值的 principled\\\n552\t    \\ justification：为什么不是 0.05 或 0.15？\\n  这个阈值是 ad hoc 还是有统计或领域基础？\\n- Rebuttal 需要补充\\\n553\t    \\ sensitivity analysis：在 0.05/0.10/0.15 三个阈值下 pattern 是否稳定\\n注意：OpenVLA 的 R² exit\\\n554\t    \\ Δ 在 v3 MCCV 修正后仅 0.033-0.086（VLA→VLA transition）， 低于 0.10 阈值。真正的 exit collapse\\\n555\t    \\ 来自 TracVLA/NORA（VLM→VLA transition, Δ=0.156-0.455）。 此实验建立了 baseline expectation，但\\\n556\t    \\ median 档位下 reviewer 会质疑 threshold choice。\\n\"\n557\t  tables:\n558\t  - title: R² Peak-Exit Comparison (OpenVLA, LIBERO-Goal)\n559\t    columns:\n560\t    - Condition\n561\t    - Peak Layer\n562\t    - Peak R²\n563\t    - Exit R²\n564\t    - Δ(peak-exit)\n565\t    rows:\n566\t    - - Trained img_mean\n567\t      - L8\n568\t      - '0.655'\n569\t      - '0.520'\n570\t      - '0.135'\n571\t    - - Trained last_pre\n572\t      - L13\n573\t      - '0.678'\n574\t      - '0.609'\n575\t      - '0.069'\n576\t    - - Untrained img_mean\n577\t      - L0\n578\t      - '0.640'\n579\t      - '0.584'\n580\t      - '0.056'\n581\t    - - Untrained last_pre\n582\t      - L32\n583\t      - '0.609'\n584\t      - '0.609'\n585\t      - '0.000'\n586\t  - title: Bootstrap Statistical Comparison\n587\t    columns:\n588\t    - Comparison\n589\t    - Δ R²\n590\t    - p-value\n591\t    - Significant?\n592\t    rows:\n593\t    - - Best-vs-best img_mean\n594\t      - '+0.015'\n595\t      - '0.006'\n596\t      - 'Yes'\n597\t    - - Best-vs-best last_pre\n598\t      - '+0.069'\n599\t      - <0.0001\n600\t      - 'Yes'\n601\t    - - Same-layer L8 img_mean\n602\t      - '+0.123'\n603\t      - <0.0001\n604\t      - 'Yes'\n605\t    - - Same-layer L13 last_pre\n606\t      - '+1.007'\n607\t      - <0.0001\n608\t      - Yes (collapsed)\n609\t  figures_description:\n610\t  - 'Per-layer R² profile: trained vs untrained, image_mean and last_preaction in\n611\t    separate panels。Trained shows inverted-U with gradual decline。Untrained shows\n612\t    deep-layer collapse (L10-L13 near zero) with L32 recovery spike。Shaded 95% CI\n613\t    bands from bootstrap。'\n614\t  analysis: 'Median 档位核心争议之一。Reviewer 3 的典型 comment： \"The Δ>0.10 threshold for ''substantial''\n615\t    exit collapse appears arbitrary. At this  threshold, OpenVLA shows collapse only\n616\t    for image_mean (Δ=0.135) but not last_preaction  (Δ=0.069). The authors should\n617\t    provide a principled justification or show that  conclusions hold across a range\n618\t    of thresholds.\"\n619\t\n620\t    Rebuttal strategy：补充 sensitivity analysis showing pattern stability at 0.05/0.10/0.15。\n621\t    At Δ>0.05：VLM→VLA 仍然 6/6，VLA→VLA 变为 2/4（Goal Δ=0.086 > 0.05）。 At Δ>0.15：VLM→VLA\n622\t    仍然 5/6（TracVLA Spatial Δ=0.138 borderline）。 二元分离（VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA）在所有阈值下基本 stable。\n623\t\n624\t    '\n625\t- name: CLIP-ViT pretraining control\n626\t  plan_id: plan_012\n627\t  description: CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP，区分 VL pretraining 贡献 vs encoder quality\n628\t  expected_results:\n629\t    projector_R2: 0.6298\n630\t    dino_cls_R2: 0.6343\n631\t    clip_cls_R2: 0.5866\n632\t    vla_image_mean_L19_R2: 0.5986\n633\t    vla_last_preaction_L19_R2: 0.6711\n634\t    ordering: last_pre > dino_cls ≈ projector > vla_img_mean > clip_cls\n635\t    clip_vs_dino_p: 0.0\n636\t  result_rationale: \"CLIP < DINO 在 RSA 和 R² 下均成立，否定了 \\\"VL pretraining dominance\\\"\\\n637\t    \\ hypothesis。 Self-supervised (DINOv2) 比 VL pretrained (CLIP) 更好地 capture action-relevant\\\n638\t    \\ structure。 Median 档位下此结果被接受，但 Reviewer 1 可能质疑： (1) CLIP ViT-L 和 DINOv2 ViT-L\\\n639\t    \\ 是不同的 architecture variants，不能 solely \\n    attribute to pretraining difference；\\n\\\n640\t    (2) SigLIP（OpenVLA 的实际 encoder）是 VL pretrained 但 RSA=0.615 > DINO=0.631，\\n   \\\n641\t    \\ 矛盾——但这通过 plan_013 branch split 解释（fused backbone 中 DINOv2 和 SigLIP \\n    贡献\\\n642\t    \\ equally）。\\n\"\n643\t  tables:\n644\t  - title: Cross-Encoder Action Probe R² (Unified Hyperparams)\n645\t    columns:\n646\t    - Encoder\n647\t    - Pretraining\n648\t    - R²\n649\t    - vs Projector p\n650\t    rows:\n651\t    - - VLA last_pre L19\n652\t      - VLA fine-tuned\n653\t      - '0.671'\n654\t      - '0.002'\n655\t    - - DINO cls_token\n656\t      - Self-supervised\n657\t      - '0.634'\n658\t      - 0.557 (n.s.)\n659\t    - - SigLIP+Projector\n660\t      - VL + projection\n661\t      - '0.630'\n662\t      - baseline\n663\t    - - VLA img_mean L19\n664\t      - VLA fine-tuned\n665\t      - '0.599'\n666\t      - <0.001\n667\t    - - CLIP cls_token\n668\t      - VL contrastive\n669\t      - '0.587'\n670\t      - <0.001\n671\t  figures_description:\n672\t  - 'Bar chart with 95% CI: R² for 5 representations。DINO ≈ Projector > CLIP clearly。last_preaction\n673\t    highest。'\n674\t  analysis: 'Clean result，全部 reviewer 接受。Median 档位下此实验的贡献是 \"supporting evidence  for\n675\t    C3 vision encoder geometry observation\"——DINOv2 ranking under RSA 在 functional  probe\n676\t    中也 partially replicated（DINO R² ≈ Projector R²）。但 CKA reversal（plan_009） 仍然 undermines\n677\t    跨 metric generalizability。\n678\t\n679\t    '\n680\t- name: Branch-split RSA (DINOv2 vs SigLIP in fused backbone)\n681\t  plan_id: plan_013\n682\t  description: 分离 DinoSigLIP fused backbone 中 DINOv2 branch vs SigLIP branch 的 RSA\n683\t    贡献\n684\t  expected_results:\n685\t    dinov2_branch_rsa: 0.619\n686\t    siglip_branch_rsa: 0.621\n687\t    fused_2176d_rsa: 0.634\n688\t    post_projector_4096d_rsa: 0.615\n689\t    standalone_dino_cls_rsa: 0.692\n690\t    standalone_dino_patch_mean_rsa: 0.631\n691\t  result_rationale: \"DINOv2 ≈ SigLIP（Δ < 0.002）在 fused backbone 中贡献 equally。 Fused\\\n692\t    \\ > either branch（complementary benefit）。Projector 从 0.634 压缩到 0.615。 Median 档位下此实验被接受为\\\n693\t    \\ clean decomposition： - Reviewer 接受 \\\"both branches contribute equally\\\" 的结论\\\n694\t    \\ - 但注意到 standalone DINO cls (0.692) > in-backbone DINOv2 branch (0.619)，\\n  差距可能来自\\\n695\t    \\ extraction layer difference（standalone = last layer，\\n  in-backbone = fused\\\n696\t    \\ intermediate）——这不是 meaningful comparison\\n- 此实验支持 C3 但 C3 已降为 observation，所以贡献有限\\n\"\n697\t  tables:\n698\t  - title: Fused Backbone Branch Decomposition\n699\t    columns:\n700\t    - Component\n701\t    - RSA (ρ)\n702\t    - Dim\n703\t    - Note\n704\t    rows:\n705\t    - - DINOv2 branch\n706\t      - '0.619'\n707\t      - '1088'\n708\t      - in-backbone\n709\t    - - SigLIP branch\n710\t      - '0.621'\n711\t      - '1088'\n712\t      - in-backbone\n713\t    - - Fused backbone\n714\t      - '0.634'\n715\t      - '2176'\n716\t      - before projection\n717\t    - - Post-projector\n718\t      - '0.615'\n719\t      - '4096'\n720\t      - LLM input\n721\t    - - Standalone DINO cls\n722\t      - '0.692'\n723\t      - '1024'\n724\t      - different layer\n725\t  figures_description:\n726\t  - 'Stacked decomposition diagram: DINOv2 (0.619) + SigLIP (0.621) → Fused (0.634)\n727\t    → Projector (0.615)。Arrows show fusion gain (+0.013) and projection loss (-0.019)。'\n728\t  analysis: Median 档位下所有 reviewer 接受。此实验的价值在 median scenario 下有限—— C3 已降为 observation，branch-split\n729\t    的精细分解不会改变 reviewer 对 core claims 的评估。 但它 demonstrates thoroughness，可能为 reviewer\n730\t    1 的正面评价贡献 \"well-executed experimental design\"。 Reviewer 3 可能在 minor comments 中建议\n731\t    \"move branch-split analysis to supplementary  to save main text space for the\n732\t    cross-architecture results which are more impactful。\"\n733\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc4ce46a-8c3b-459f-bd12-119e3d710a0a","uuid":"520262dc-f3fd-4266-947e-3373fd3bcc45","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:25:04.053Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260527T022433/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Exit collapse + routing gradient 保持为 core findings（reviewer acceptance\n  ~75%）， CF sensitivity 降为 \"supporting evidence with caveats\"（acceptance ~45%）。 1-2\n  位 reviewer 指出 metric incomparability（trained Cohen''s d vs untrained cosine dist）\n  使 amplification 的定量化不可靠，要求 behavioral validation 作为 representational claims 的补充。\n  Rebuttal 需要：(1) Δ>0.10 阈值 sensitivity analysis，(2) 诚实回应 behavioral gap， (3) 将 CF\n  从 \"core finding\" 重新定位为 \"consistent observation\"。 预计 reviewer_avg ~6.0，accept_prob\n  ~0.35，rebuttal_success ~0.50。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: SigLIP+Projector RSA baseline\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO — 证明 action-relevant 结构源自\n    frozen vision encoder\n  expected_results:\n    siglip_projector_rsa: 0.6153\n    bootstrap_95_ci:\n    - 0.5257\n    - 0.6954\n    trained_vla_peak_rsa: 0.4876\n    untrained_vla_peak_rsa: 0.4846\n    dino_rsa: 0.388\n    llm_degradation_magnitude: 0.127\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档位下此实验被全部 reviewer 接受（A1 holds）。RSA=0.615 >> VLA 0.488\n    的 gap 清晰建立了 \"vision encoder 是 action-relevant structure 的主要来源\" 这一非争议性结论。 但 1 位\n    reviewer 会注意到这是 RSA metric 下的结论——CKA 下 ordering 不同（plan_009 结果）。 此实验对 C1 framework\n    贡献最大，不涉及 median 档位的核心争议点（CF metric incomparability）。 CI 较宽 [0.526, 0.695] 会被提及但不作为\n    major concern，因为 point estimate 远高于 VLA peak。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Action-Relevant Structure Source Decomposition\n    columns:\n    - Representation\n    - RSA (ρ)\n    - 95% CI\n    - vs DINO\n    rows:\n    - - SigLIP+Projector\n      - '0.615'\n      - '[0.526, 0.695]'\n      - '+0.227'\n    - - VLA Trained Peak (L9)\n      - '0.488'\n      - —\n      - '+0.100'\n    - - VLA Untrained Peak (L12)\n      - '0.485'\n      - —\n      - '+0.097'\n    - - DINO cls_token\n      - '0.388'\n      - —\n      - baseline\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: RSA values for SigLIP projector > VLA trained ≈ VLA untrained >> DINO,\n    with 95% CI error bars。清晰的三级阶梯。'\n  analysis: 'Reviewer 共识：frozen encoder dominance 不争议。但 median 档位下 Reviewer 2 可能指出\n    \"LLM degradation\" 的措辞过强——LLM 同时在做 instruction routing 和 action computation， RSA\n    下降可能反映功能转换而非信息丢失。建议用 \"geometric reorganization\" 替代 \"degradation\"。 此实验在 rebuttal\n    中无需调整。\n\n    '\n- name: DINO standalone baseline\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: DINOv2 baseline RSA — standalone vision model 参照\n  expected_results:\n    temporal_distance_rho_pooled: 0.833\n    per_task_rho_mean: 0.9008\n    R2: 0.687\n    subtask_macro_auc: 0.9717\n    control_b_permutation_rho: 0.039\n  result_rationale: 'Clean baseline，无争议。DINO RSA=0.388 远低于 VLA 和 projector，建立了 architecture\n    gap。 Subtask AUC=0.97 被 reviewer 接受但会引发 \"goals are visually distinguishable\" 的注意，\n    这在后续 goal classification experiments 中成为 confound（10-way classification trivially\n    easy）。 Median 档位下此实验本身不受挑战，但 reviewer 会用它来质疑后续 probe 实验的 discriminability。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: DINOv2 Standalone Performance\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Value\n    - Note\n    rows:\n    - - Temporal ρ (per-task)\n      - '0.901'\n      - correct baseline\n    - - Action Probe R²\n      - '0.687'\n      - vision-only ceiling\n    - - Subtask AUC\n      - '0.972'\n      - visually distinguishable\n    - - Permutation Control ρ\n      - '0.039'\n      - validates signal\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter: predicted vs actual temporal distance，per-task colored。High correlation\n    but cross-task variance visible。'\n  analysis: '所有 reviewer 接受。用于建立 DINO < SigLIP < VLA trained 的 ordering baseline。\n    Median 档位下唯一风险：Reviewer 3 可能质疑 DINOv2 作为 baseline 的 fairness （DINOv2 是 ViT-L/14\n    1024d vs VLA 4096d），但 dimension mismatch 在 RSA/CKA 中 不是 confound（metric 对 dimensionality\n    invariant）。\n\n    '\n- name: Per-layer RSA degradation curve\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: Per-layer RSA curve — 追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的变换轨迹\n  expected_results:\n    trained_image_mean_peak_layer: 9\n    trained_image_mean_peak_rsa: 0.4876\n    untrained_image_mean_peak_layer: 12\n    untrained_image_mean_peak_rsa: 0.4846\n    proj_to_l1_drop_trained: 0.2036\n    proj_to_l1_drop_untrained: 0.1512\n    trained_pattern: non_monotonic (inverted-U)\n    untrained_pattern: non_monotonic\n  result_rationale: 'Inverted-U pattern 是 C3 的核心 evidence。Median 档位下（A3 fails 的延伸）：\n    (1) rise phase Δρ=+0.016 被 1 位 reviewer 认为 negligible（CI includes 0）， inverted-U\n    的 \"rise\" 部分可能只是 noise； (2) CKA 下 pattern 完全不同（monotonic），reviewer 质疑 \"non-monotonic\n    refinement\"  是 metric-specific artifact； (3) decline phase Δρ=-0.206 更 robust，但\n    reviewer 要求在正文（非 appendix）承认 metric dependence。 最终 C3 作为 \"qualified observation\n    under RSA\" 存活，但不贡献于 core claims。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Per-Layer RSA Profile Summary\n    columns:\n    - Condition\n    - Peak Layer\n    - Peak RSA\n    - Proj→L1 Drop\n    - Pattern\n    rows:\n    - - Trained (with inst)\n      - L9\n      - '0.488'\n      - '-0.204'\n      - inverted-U\n    - - Untrained (with inst)\n      - L12\n      - '0.485'\n      - '-0.151'\n      - non-monotonic\n    - - Trained (no inst)\n      - L30\n      - '0.489'\n      - '-0.253'\n      - increasing\n    - - Untrained (no inst)\n      - L6\n      - '0.480'\n      - '-0.137'\n      - non-monotonic\n  figures_description:\n  - '33-layer RSA profile plot: 4 conditions overlaid。Trained shows inverted-U with\n    peak at L9-L12, untrained flatter。Projector output (0.615) as horizontal dashed\n    line shows all LLM layers below projector。'\n  analysis: 'Median 档位 Reviewer 2 的典型批评：\"The inverted-U pattern is only demonstrated\n    under RSA.  CKA shows monotonic increase (plan_009), which directly contradicts\n    the ''non-monotonic refinement''  narrative. The authors should either demonstrate\n    metric-robustness or downgrade this to an observation.\" Response：承认并降级为 observation。Rebuttal\n    可补充 R² functional probe 也显示 inverted-U （plan_011），但 reviewer 可能 counter：\"R² measures\n    decodability, not geometry — different construct。\"\n\n    '\n- name: Output head analysis (frozen encoder verification)\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: SigLIP+projector frozen 确认, LLM 权重变化不传导到视觉表征\n  expected_results:\n    vision_cos_sim: 1.0\n    vision_rel_change: 0.0\n    projector_cos_sim: 1.001\n    projector_rel_change: 0.0\n    llm_mean_rel_change: 1.316\n    llm_range:\n    - 1.22\n    - 1.37\n    head_vs_llm_ratio: 1.12\n    shallow_adaptation_gate: FAIL (1.12x < 3x threshold)\n  result_rationale: '此实验确认 vision backbone + projector 在 trained 和 untrained 之间完全一致（cos_sim=1.0），\n    解释了为什么 RSA 在 image_mean tokens 上 trained ≈ untrained。Median 档位下被接受 （A1 holds），但\n    reviewer 注意到 caveat：\"comparison is pretrained Llama vs random init,  not pre/post\n    fine-tuning\"，这限制了 interpretability。LLM weights uniformly distributed （ratio=1.12x）否定了\n    shallow adaptation hypothesis——head 不特殊。 此实验支持 C1 framework 的 \"frozen encoder\"\n    前提，不涉及 median 档位的争议点。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Weight Divergence by Module Group\n    columns:\n    - Module\n    - Count\n    - Mean Rel Change\n    - Cos Sim\n    - Verdict\n    rows:\n    - - Vision Backbone\n      - '685'\n      - '0.000'\n      - '1.000'\n      - IDENTICAL\n    - - Projector\n      - '6'\n      - '0.000'\n      - '1.001'\n      - IDENTICAL\n    - - LLM Layers\n      - '288'\n      - '1.316'\n      - '0.218'\n      - DIVERGED\n    - - LM Head\n      - '1'\n      - '1.475'\n      - '0.000'\n      - DIVERGED\n    - - Embedding\n      - '1'\n      - '1.329'\n      - '-0.000'\n      - DIVERGED\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: rel_change per LLM layer (L0-L31)，showing uniform ~1.3 across all layers，no\n    depth gradient。Vision/projector rows blank (zero change)。'\n  analysis: '全部 reviewer 接受。此实验为 C1 framework 提供了必要的 architectural verification。 Median\n    档位下无额外挑战。但 Reviewer 1 可能在 minor comments 中建议 \"clarify that  untrained = random\n    init, not ablated weights\" 以避免读者误解。\n\n    '\n- name: 6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks (orphaned)\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 系统性验证 trained ≈ untrained across 6 methods\n  expected_results:\n    status: orphaned\n    conclusion: 'All 6 methods consistent: trained ≈ untrained >> DINO'\n    note: 被后续更精细的实验取代（plan_011 fulllayer R², d041 definitive RSA, etc.）\n  result_rationale: '此实验在 Phase 1 被 orphaned，其核心结论（trained ≈ untrained in RSA/R²）被后续实验\n    独立复现。在 median 档位下不直接贡献，但其 \"trained ≈ untrained\" 的 RSA 结论正是 reviewer 用来质疑 \"training\n    effect\" narrative 的弹药之一——如果 training 不改变 RSA， 那 training 到底做了什么？Answer 在 C2（routing\n    reorganization），但 reviewer 可能认为 证据不够 conclusive without behavioral validation（A4\n    partially fails）。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Orphaned，不进入论文。但其结论（trained ≈ untrained）被 plan_007 和 d041 复现， 成为 C3 \"observation\"\n    而非 \"finding\" 的证据基础。\n\n    '\n- name: Instruction ablation RSA\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 去掉 instruction text 测 RSA 变化\n  expected_results:\n    with_inst_untrained_peak_rsa: 0.4846\n    no_inst_untrained_peak_rsa: 0.4802\n    delta: 0.0044\n    gate_threshold: 0.1\n    gate_judgment: FAIL — Δ=0.004 << 0.10\n  result_rationale: 'Negative result：移除 instruction 对 image token RSA 几乎无影响（Δ=0.004\n    << 0.10）。 这证明了 action-relevant structure 是 vision-driven 而非 instruction-driven。\n    Median 档位下此结论被接受（支持 C1 \"image tokens 不 attend to instructions\" 的验证）， 但 reviewer\n    可能指出：这只说明 image_mean RSA 不依赖 instruction，不能推广到 last_preaction tokens（C2 的核心 readout\n    position）。实际上 last_preaction 的 routing 完全依赖 instruction（cross-instruction probe\n    100%），两个 readout 位置的 independence pattern 不同——这本身是一个 finding，但需要在论文中明确区分。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Instruction Ablation Effect on RSA\n    columns:\n    - Condition\n    - Peak RSA\n    - Δ vs with-inst\n    rows:\n    - - Untrained + instruction\n      - '0.485'\n      - baseline\n    - - Untrained − instruction\n      - '0.480'\n      - '-0.004'\n    - - Threshold for significance\n      - —\n      - '0.10'\n    - - DINO baseline\n      - '0.388'\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Per-layer RSA curves: with-instruction vs without-instruction overlay，几乎完全重合。DINO\n    horizontal line 远低于两者。'\n  analysis: 'Reviewer 接受。此 negative result 实际强化了 C1：image tokens 的 action-relevant  geometry\n    来自 visual content，instruction presence 不影响。但 median 档位下  Reviewer 2 会追问：\"if instruction\n    doesn''t matter for image tokens, what exactly  does VLA training change?\" — 这个问题的答案在\n    C2（routing at instruction token positions）， 但需要更清晰的 framing。\n\n    '\n- name: 2×2 training × instruction matrix\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 四条件全收敛验证 — trained/untrained × with/without instruction\n  expected_results:\n    trained_with_inst: 0.4876\n    trained_no_inst: 0.489\n    untrained_with_inst: 0.4846\n    untrained_no_inst: 0.4802\n    bootstrap_delta_ci: '[-0.058, 0.072] includes 0'\n    max_pairwise_delta: 0.0088\n    dino_baseline: 0.388\n  result_rationale: \"2×2 matrix 所有 4 cells 收敛在 0.480-0.489 的窄带中，bootstrap CI 包含 0。\\\n    \\ 这是 C3 \\\"instruction invariance\\\" observation 的定量基础。Median 档位下被接受 但 reviewer\\\n    \\ 的解读分歧： - Reviewer 1：接受，认为 \\\"vision encoder geometry dominates\\\" 是 clean result\\\n    \\ - Reviewer 2：认为这意味着 \\\"neither training nor instruction has meaningful effect\\\n    \\ \\n  on image token geometry\\\"，进而质疑论文的 novelty——如果训练不改变 RSA，论文需要\\n  更强地论证 routing/R²\\\n    \\ 变化的意义\\n- Reviewer 3：接受，但要求将此与 C2 的 exit collapse（R² 层面的变化）明确对比——\\n  RSA 不变但\\\n    \\ R² 变化说明 \\\"geometry preserved but decodability reorganized\\\"\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: '2×2 Factorial Design: RSA Convergence'\n    columns:\n    - ''\n    - With Instruction\n    - Without Instruction\n    - Instruction Effect\n    rows:\n    - - Trained\n      - '0.488'\n      - '0.489'\n      - '-0.001'\n    - - Untrained\n      - '0.485'\n      - '0.480'\n      - '+0.004'\n    - - Training Effect\n      - '+0.003'\n      - '+0.009'\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - '2×2 interaction plot: RSA on y-axis (range 0.47-0.50), training on x-axis, instruction\n    as separate lines。Lines nearly flat and overlapping — no main effects, no interaction。DINO\n    at 0.388 shown as reference。'\n  analysis: 'Median 档位的关键 pivot point。此实验的 \"null result\"（4 条件无差异）在 median  scenario\n    下被部分 reviewer 视为 limitation：\"if your framework can''t detect training  effects\n    in RSA, perhaps RSA is the wrong metric。\" 这直接导致 C3 从 core claim  降为 observation。Rebuttal\n    需要论证：RSA invariance + R² divergence = geometry-function  dissociation，这本身是 interesting，但需要\n    behavioral evidence 来确认 functional significance。\n\n    '\n- name: Random instruction control (content invariance)\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 用 random/shuffled/empty instruction 替代真实 instruction 测 RSA 变化\n  expected_results:\n    normal_peak_rsa: 0.4888\n    random_peak_rsa: 0.4835\n    shuffled_peak_rsa: 0.4832\n    empty_peak_rsa: 0.4723\n    max_absolute_delta: 0.0165\n    instruction_invariant: true\n  result_rationale: '三重不变性完备验证：training invariance（plan_007）+ instruction presence\n    invariance （plan_006）+ instruction content invariance（此实验）。所有 delta < 0.017。 Median\n    档位下被全部 reviewer 接受为 thorough control。这实际上强化了 C1 framework 的可信度——image token geometry\n    对 instruction content 完全不敏感。 但 reviewer 会对比 counterfactual sensitivity results（C2-X\n    CF）：image tokens 对 instruction invariant，但 instruction/last_preaction tokens 高度\n    sensitive（d≥0.45）。 这个 dissociation 本身是 interesting，但在 median 档位下被认为 \"consistent\n    with  causal mask — not surprising。\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Instruction Content Invariance (Trained Model)\n    columns:\n    - Instruction Type\n    - Peak RSA\n    - Δ vs Normal\n    rows:\n    - - Normal (correct)\n      - '0.489'\n      - baseline\n    - - Random tokens\n      - '0.484'\n      - '-0.005'\n    - - Shuffled words\n      - '0.483'\n      - '-0.006'\n    - - Empty string\n      - '0.472'\n      - '-0.017'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Per-layer RSA curves: 4 instruction conditions overlaid。All curves within ±0.017\n    band。Peak layers identical (L16)。'\n  analysis: 'Uncontroversial control。所有 reviewer 认为此实验 demonstrates thoroughness。\n    Median 档位下唯一 minor concern：empty string Δ=-0.017 是 4 条件中最大的， 暗示 instruction presence\n    有微弱效应（token count/position effect），但远低于 threshold。\n\n    '\n- name: CKA verification (metric robustness)\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: 用 CKA 指标重复 RSA 发现，确保不是指标依赖\n  expected_results:\n    linear_cka_ordering: untrained > trained > projector > DINO\n    rdm_cka_ordering: trained > projector > untrained > DINO\n    rsa_ordering: projector >> trained ≈ untrained >> DINO\n    cka_reversal_detected: true\n    dino_lowest_robust: true\n    last_preaction_highest: 0.127\n  result_rationale: '这是 median 档位的关键 problematic experiment。CKA ordering 与 RSA 反转——\n    CKA 下 untrained > trained（RSA 下 trained ≈ untrained），projector 不再最高。 这直接导致： (1)\n    C3 的 \"non-monotonic refinement\" 仅在 RSA 下成立，metric-dependent； (2) DINOv2 \"highest\n    geometric foundation\" 仅在 RSA 下成立； (3) 1-2 位 reviewer 认为 RSA 结果不可推广。 但 DINO 在所有\n    metrics 下均最低（robust），且 last_preaction >> image_mean 的 redistribution pattern 在\n    CKA 下也成立。 A2 partially 的表现：exit collapse 主要基于 R²（functional metric），不依赖 RSA/CKA，\n    所以 exit collapse 本身不受 CKA reversal 影响。但 C3 vision encoder geometry claim  被严重\n    undercut。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: RSA vs CKA Metric Comparison\n    columns:\n    - Representation\n    - RSA (ρ)\n    - Linear CKA\n    - RDM-CKA\n    - Consistent?\n    rows:\n    - - SigLIP Projector\n      - '0.615'\n      - '0.081'\n      - '0.257'\n      - No — RSA >> CKA\n    - - VLA Trained (img_mean)\n      - '0.488'\n      - '0.083'\n      - '0.260'\n      - 'No'\n    - - VLA Untrained (img_mean)\n      - '0.485'\n      - '0.089'\n      - '0.246'\n      - No — CKA reversal\n    - - DINO cls_token\n      - '0.388'\n      - '0.066'\n      - '0.241'\n      - Yes — lowest in all\n    - - VLA Trained (last_pre)\n      - —\n      - '0.127'\n      - '0.290'\n      - Highest in CKA\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Side-by-side bar charts: RSA ordering (projector > trained ≈ untrained > DINO)\n    vs CKA ordering (untrained > trained > projector > DINO for linear CKA)。Visual\n    对比 highlights reversal。'\n  analysis: 'Median 档位核心 attack surface。Reviewer 2 的典型评论： \"The RSA-CKA dissociation\n    undermines confidence in the geometric interpretation.  The authors claim ''non-monotonic\n    refinement'' based on RSA, but CKA shows monotonic  structure. This metric dependence\n    should be acknowledged as a fundamental limitation,  not relegated to an appendix.\"\n    Rebuttal 策略：承认 dissociation，将 C3 降为 \"observation under RSA\"，强调 C2 （exit collapse,\n    routing）基于 R² functional probe，不依赖 RSA/CKA 选择。 Reviewer acceptance for C3 drops\n    to ~0.4，但 C2 不受影响（~0.75）。\n\n    '\n- name: LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark replication\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 第三个 benchmark 交叉验证 RSA inverted-U 和 R² patterns\n  expected_results:\n    rsa_trained_img_peak:\n      layer: 14\n      rsa: 0.691\n    rsa_trained_lastpre_peak:\n      layer: 15\n      rsa: 0.695\n    rsa_untrained_img_peak:\n      layer: 0\n      rsa: 0.652\n    r2_trained_img_peak:\n      layer: 13\n      R2: 0.696\n    r2_trained_lastpre_peak:\n      layer: 21\n      R2: 0.675\n    r2_untrained_img_peak:\n      layer: 0\n      R2: 0.673\n    bootstrap_p: <0.001 for all trained vs untrained\n    cross_benchmark_consistency: high — peak layers within 2-layer range\n  result_rationale: 'LIBERO-Spatial 复现了 LIBERO-Goal 的所有核心 patterns：trained inverted-U,  untrained\n    flat/declining, bootstrap significant。Peak layers 一致（Goal L8-L13,  Spatial L13-L21）。Median\n    档位下此实验强化了 within-OpenVLA 的 reproducibility， 被 reviewer 接受。但 reviewer 会注意到： (1)\n    仍然是同一架构（OpenVLA），跨架构验证更重要（D088-D094 addresses this）； (2) RSA inverted-U 的 rise\n    phase 在 Spatial 中 Δρ=0.039（Goal 中 0.016）， 略更 robust 但仍在 metric-dependent 的质疑范围内。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Cross-Benchmark Replication (Goal vs Spatial)\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Goal Peak\n    - Spatial Peak\n    - Δ Layers\n    rows:\n    - - RSA trained img_mean\n      - L12 (0.628)\n      - L14 (0.691)\n      - '+2'\n    - - RSA trained last_pre\n      - L12 (0.643)\n      - L15 (0.695)\n      - '+3'\n    - - R² trained img_mean\n      - L8 (0.655)\n      - L13 (0.696)\n      - '+5'\n    - - R² trained last_pre\n      - L13 (0.678)\n      - L21 (0.675)\n      - '+8'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Dual-panel per-layer profile: Goal (left) vs Spatial (right), with RSA and R²\n    curves overlaid。Both show inverted-U for trained condition。Peak layers marked\n    with vertical lines。'\n  analysis: 'Reviewer 接受 cross-benchmark replication。Median 档位下 Reviewer 1 可能评价： \"Good\n    that patterns replicate across task suites, but both are within the same  model\n    (OpenVLA). The cross-architecture validation (TracVLA, NORA) is more convincing  for\n    the generalization claim.\" 此实验对 A1 holds 贡献但不是 decisive。\n\n    '\n- name: Full-layer R² scan (132 probes)\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: 33 layers × 2 conditions × 2 aggregations — R² per-layer curve 验证 exit\n    collapse\n  expected_results:\n    trained_image_mean_peak:\n      layer: 8\n      R2: 0.6553\n    trained_last_preaction_peak:\n      layer: 13\n      R2: 0.6779\n    untrained_image_mean_peak:\n      layer: 0\n      R2: 0.6403\n    untrained_last_preaction_peak:\n      layer: 32\n      R2: 0.6093\n    bootstrap_best_vs_best_imgmean:\n      delta: 0.015\n      p: 0.006\n    bootstrap_best_vs_best_lastpre:\n      delta: 0.069\n      p: 0.0001\n    untrained_L10_L13_collapse: R² near -0.33 (pathological)\n  result_rationale: \"此实验是 C2 exit collapse 的 foundational evidence（OpenVLA 内部）。 Trained\\\n    \\ last_preaction 显示经典 inverted-U：L13 peak 0.678 → L32 exit 0.609（Δ=0.069）。 Untrained\\\n    \\ 则 L10-L13 完全 collapse（R² ≈ -0.33），仅 L32 恢复到 0.609。\\nMedian 档位下（A2 partially）：\\\n    \\ - Exit collapse pattern 被接受（3/4 reviewers） - 但 Reviewer 3 质疑 Δ>0.10 阈值的 principled\\\n    \\ justification：为什么不是 0.05 或 0.15？\\n  这个阈值是 ad hoc 还是有统计或领域基础？\\n- Rebuttal 需要补充\\\n    \\ sensitivity analysis：在 0.05/0.10/0.15 三个阈值下 pattern 是否稳定\\n注意：OpenVLA 的 R² exit\\\n    \\ Δ 在 v3 MCCV 修正后仅 0.033-0.086（VLA→VLA transition）， 低于 0.10 阈值。真正的 exit collapse\\\n    \\ 来自 TracVLA/NORA（VLM→VLA transition, Δ=0.156-0.455）。 此实验建立了 baseline expectation，但\\\n    \\ median 档位下 reviewer 会质疑 threshold choice。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: R² Peak-Exit Comparison (OpenVLA, LIBERO-Goal)\n    columns:\n    - Condition\n    - Peak Layer\n    - Peak R²\n    - Exit R²\n    - Δ(peak-exit)\n    rows:\n    - - Trained img_mean\n      - L8\n      - '0.655'\n      - '0.520'\n      - '0.135'\n    - - Trained last_pre\n      - L13\n      - '0.678'\n      - '0.609'\n      - '0.069'\n    - - Untrained img_mean\n      - L0\n      - '0.640'\n      - '0.584'\n      - '0.056'\n    - - Untrained last_pre\n      - L32\n      - '0.609'\n      - '0.609'\n      - '0.000'\n  - title: Bootstrap Statistical Comparison\n    columns:\n    - Comparison\n    - Δ R²\n    - p-value\n    - Significant?\n    rows:\n    - - Best-vs-best img_mean\n      - '+0.015'\n      - '0.006'\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - Best-vs-best last_pre\n      - '+0.069'\n      - <0.0001\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - Same-layer L8 img_mean\n      - '+0.123'\n      - <0.0001\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - Same-layer L13 last_pre\n      - '+1.007'\n      - <0.0001\n      - Yes (collapsed)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Per-layer R² profile: trained vs untrained, image_mean and last_preaction in\n    separate panels。Trained shows inverted-U with gradual decline。Untrained shows\n    deep-layer collapse (L10-L13 near zero) with L32 recovery spike。Shaded 95% CI\n    bands from bootstrap。'\n  analysis: 'Median 档位核心争议之一。Reviewer 3 的典型 comment： \"The Δ>0.10 threshold for ''substantial''\n    exit collapse appears arbitrary. At this  threshold, OpenVLA shows collapse only\n    for image_mean (Δ=0.135) but not last_preaction  (Δ=0.069). The authors should\n    provide a principled justification or show that  conclusions hold across a range\n    of thresholds.\"\n\n    Rebuttal strategy：补充 sensitivity analysis showing pattern stability at 0.05/0.10/0.15。\n    At Δ>0.05：VLM→VLA 仍然 6/6，VLA→VLA 变为 2/4（Goal Δ=0.086 > 0.05）。 At Δ>0.15：VLM→VLA\n    仍然 5/6（TracVLA Spatial Δ=0.138 borderline）。 二元分离（VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA）在所有阈值下基本 stable。\n\n    '\n- name: CLIP-ViT pretraining control\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP，区分 VL pretraining 贡献 vs encoder quality\n  expected_results:\n    projector_R2: 0.6298\n    dino_cls_R2: 0.6343\n    clip_cls_R2: 0.5866\n    vla_image_mean_L19_R2: 0.5986\n    vla_last_preaction_L19_R2: 0.6711\n    ordering: last_pre > dino_cls ≈ projector > vla_img_mean > clip_cls\n    clip_vs_dino_p: 0.0\n  result_rationale: \"CLIP < DINO 在 RSA 和 R² 下均成立，否定了 \\\"VL pretraining dominance\\\"\\\n    \\ hypothesis。 Self-supervised (DINOv2) 比 VL pretrained (CLIP) 更好地 capture action-relevant\\\n    \\ structure。 Median 档位下此结果被接受，但 Reviewer 1 可能质疑： (1) CLIP ViT-L 和 DINOv2 ViT-L\\\n    \\ 是不同的 architecture variants，不能 solely \\n    attribute to pretraining difference；\\n\\\n    (2) SigLIP（OpenVLA 的实际 encoder）是 VL pretrained 但 RSA=0.615 > DINO=0.631，\\n   \\\n    \\ 矛盾——但这通过 plan_013 branch split 解释（fused backbone 中 DINOv2 和 SigLIP \\n    贡献\\\n    \\ equally）。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: Cross-Encoder Action Probe R² (Unified Hyperparams)\n    columns:\n    - Encoder\n    - Pretraining\n    - R²\n    - vs Projector p\n    rows:\n    - - VLA last_pre L19\n      - VLA fine-tuned\n      - '0.671'\n      - '0.002'\n    - - DINO cls_token\n      - Self-supervised\n      - '0.634'\n      - 0.557 (n.s.)\n    - - SigLIP+Projector\n      - VL + projection\n      - '0.630'\n      - baseline\n    - - VLA img_mean L19\n      - VLA fine-tuned\n      - '0.599'\n      - <0.001\n    - - CLIP cls_token\n      - VL contrastive\n      - '0.587'\n      - <0.001\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart with 95% CI: R² for 5 representations。DINO ≈ Projector > CLIP clearly。last_preaction\n    highest。'\n  analysis: 'Clean result，全部 reviewer 接受。Median 档位下此实验的贡献是 \"supporting evidence  for\n    C3 vision encoder geometry observation\"——DINOv2 ranking under RSA 在 functional  probe\n    中也 partially replicated（DINO R² ≈ Projector R²）。但 CKA reversal（plan_009） 仍然 undermines\n    跨 metric generalizability。\n\n    '\n- name: Branch-split RSA (DINOv2 vs SigLIP in fused backbone)\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: 分离 DinoSigLIP fused backbone 中 DINOv2 branch vs SigLIP branch 的 RSA\n    贡献\n  expected_results:\n    dinov2_branch_rsa: 0.619\n    siglip_branch_rsa: 0.621\n    fused_2176d_rsa: 0.634\n    post_projector_4096d_rsa: 0.615\n    standalone_dino_cls_rsa: 0.692\n    standalone_dino_patch_mean_rsa: 0.631\n  result_rationale: \"DINOv2 ≈ SigLIP（Δ < 0.002）在 fused backbone 中贡献 equally。 Fused\\\n    \\ > either branch（complementary benefit）。Projector 从 0.634 压缩到 0.615。 Median 档位下此实验被接受为\\\n    \\ clean decomposition： - Reviewer 接受 \\\"both branches contribute equally\\\" 的结论\\\n    \\ - 但注意到 standalone DINO cls (0.692) > in-backbone DINOv2 branch (0.619)，\\n  差距可能来自\\\n    \\ extraction layer difference（standalone = last layer，\\n  in-backbone = fused\\\n    \\ intermediate）——这不是 meaningful comparison\\n- 此实验支持 C3 但 C3 已降为 observation，所以贡献有限\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - title: Fused Backbone Branch Decomposition\n    columns:\n    - Component\n    - RSA (ρ)\n    - Dim\n    - Note\n    rows:\n    - - DINOv2 branch\n      - '0.619'\n      - '1088'\n      - in-backbone\n    - - SigLIP branch\n      - '0.621'\n      - '1088'\n      - in-backbone\n    - - Fused backbone\n      - '0.634'\n      - '2176'\n      - before projection\n    - - Post-projector\n      - '0.615'\n      - '4096'\n      - LLM input\n    - - Standalone DINO cls\n      - '0.692'\n      - '1024'\n      - different layer\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Stacked decomposition diagram: DINOv2 (0.619) + SigLIP (0.621) → Fused (0.634)\n    → Projector (0.615)。Arrows show fusion gain (+0.013) and projection loss (-0.019)。'\n  analysis: Median 档位下所有 reviewer 接受。此实验的价值在 median scenario 下有限—— C3 已降为 observation，branch-split\n    的精细分解不会改变 reviewer 对 core claims 的评估。 但它 demonstrates thoroughness，可能为 reviewer\n    1 的正面评价贡献 \"well-executed experimental design\"。 Reviewer 3 可能在 minor comments 中建议\n    \"move branch-split analysis to supplementary  to save main text space for the\n    cross-architecture results which are more impactful。\"\n","numLines":733,"startLine":1,"totalLines":733}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T4cr4zTRwKzEJJ7Dxw22sA","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026, though the specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form details are limited in the current results. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Reviewer Information\n\nAll submissions to CoRL 2026 must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer and is qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nCoRL aims to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Related Review Standards\n\nWhile specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines aren't fully detailed in these results, the search found that previous versions of CoRL (such as CoRL 2024) included evaluation of submissions based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nFor more detailed and official CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form specifics, I recommend:\n1. Checking the official CoRL 2026 website at https://www.corl.org/\n2. Visiting the OpenReview page at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference\n3. Contacting the CoRL 2026 organizers directly\n\nThe guidelines may not yet be publicly available if the review process hasn't officially started.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc4ce46a-8c3b-459f-bd12-119e3d710a0a","uuid":"ec3c1d2d-945f-481f-9566-c5ce73c1bec1","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:25:05.718Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01K5Y5iqGWbTP42G5wFqr4Dg","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026, though the specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form details are limited in the current results. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Reviewer Information\n\nAll submissions to CoRL 2026 must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer and is qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nCoRL aims to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Related Review Standards\n\nWhile specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines aren't fully detailed in these results, the search found that previous versions of CoRL (such as CoRL 2024) included evaluation of submissions based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nFor more detailed and official CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form specifics, I recommend:\n1. Checking the official CoRL 2026 website at https://www.corl.org/\n2. Visiting the OpenReview page at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference\n3. Contacting the CoRL 2026 organizers directly\n\nThe guidelines may not yet be publicly available if the review process hasn't officially started."],"durationSeconds":5.885533317000001}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011yB4nf5U2E6R33zaBb5XGq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056528/\"},{\"title\":\"Can LLM feedback enhance review quality? A randomized study of 20K   reviews at ICLR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.09737\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2024 reviewer guidelines, but not specifically for CoRL 2025. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2024 Reviewer Guidelines\n\nRegular paper submissions at CoRL are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\nAll CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through either explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nThe search results provided information from CoRL 2024 rather than the specific 2025 guidelines you requested. If you need the official CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines with the complete scoring criteria and review form details, I'd recommend checking the official CoRL 2025 conference website directly, as the full 2025 guidelines may not yet be widely indexed online.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc4ce46a-8c3b-459f-bd12-119e3d710a0a","uuid":"920748c8-638e-449f-9404-da45ff2dd667","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:25:07.003Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01XdZngFuwCNARLziJeuCR3U","content":[{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056528/"},{"title":"Can LLM feedback enhance review quality? A randomized study of 20K   reviews at ICLR 2025","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.09737"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2024 reviewer guidelines, but not specifically for CoRL 2025. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2024 Reviewer Guidelines\n\nRegular paper submissions at CoRL are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\nAll CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through either explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nThe search results provided information from CoRL 2024 rather than the specific 2025 guidelines you requested. If you need the official CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines with the complete scoring criteria and review form details, I'd recommend checking the official CoRL 2025 conference website directly, as the full 2025 guidelines may not yet be widely indexed online."],"durationSeconds":6.699438395000001}}
