{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QG3Xm2ogHiApsNgttFPbPU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL openreview review form \"overall score\" \"1:\" \"10:\" recommendation scale robot learning\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Workshop Robot Data | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FWorkshop%2FRobot_Data\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Reward Functions from Scale Feedback\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.00284\"}]\n\nI found some information about CoRL's reviewer guidelines and instructions, but the search results don't contain the specific details about the OpenReview review form's \"overall score\" scale with \"1:\" to \"10:\" notation and recommendation scale. Let me perform a more targeted search.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Default Review Form | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701\"},{\"title\":\"Why are the \\\"rating\\\" and \\\"confidence\\\" fields in my PC Console wrong? | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/getting-started/frequently-asked-questions/why-are-the-rating-and-confidence-fields-in-my-pc-console-wrong\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found information about OpenReview's default review form structure, though the specific CoRL review form details weren't fully captured. Here's what I found:\n\nOpenReview's default review form includes a rating scale with values from 10 down to 4, where 10 represents \"Top 5% of accepted papers, seminal paper\", 9 represents \"Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept\", 8 represents \"Top 50% of accepted papers, clear accept\", 7 represents \"Good paper, accept\", 6 represents \"Marginally above acceptance threshold\", 5 represents \"Marginally below acceptance threshold\", and 4 represents \"Ok but not good enough\".\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain the complete specific information about CoRL's exact OpenReview review form with the precise \"1:\" to \"10:\" overall score scale and recommendation categories you're looking for. To get the exact details of CoRL's review form, you may need to:\n\n1. Check the actual CoRL OpenReview page directly during an active submission period\n2. Look at the CoRL reviewer guidelines page for the specific year you're interested in\n3. Contact the CoRL program chairs directly\n\nWould you like me to search for information about a specific year of CoRL (such as CoRL 2024 or 2025)?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc4ce46a-8c3b-459f-bd12-119e3d710a0a","uuid":"ff24f97e-9081-4d8c-9259-2baf998dfc14","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:25:32.012Z","to